EXIT 1
STDOUT 0

STDERR 686
tests/error_method_receiver_cannot_be_a_polymorphic_argument.glos:1:10: Error: The name 'this' is reserved for the receiver argument of a method, and therefore cannot be defined here

    foo :: ($this: Foo)

    This is the first argument in what looks to be a function. Normally this is perfectly valid and would define
    the function as a method. However, this argument seems to be directly polymorphic, which is not allowed.

    The receiver can have a polymorphic type, but the argument itself cannot be polymorphic.

        foo :: (this: Foo($T)) {}    // This is allowed
        bar :: ($this: Bar)    {}    // This is not (Notice the difference in the position of the '$')


